Subject: [PATCH] PER: keep extensibility of class field types under table constraints

Problem: a component typed as a class field reference with only a table
constraint, e.g.

    PoiType ::= INTEGER(1..128,...)
    BLOCK-TYPE ::= CLASS { &id PoiType, &Content } ...
    WrappedPoiInformationBlock ::= SEQUENCE {
        poiType  BLOCK-TYPE.&id({PoiInformationSet}), ...

was generated as (1..128) without APC_EXTENSIBLE. asn1constraint_pullup()
removes the parent's extension markers whenever the component has its own
constraint, but table constraints are not PER-visible (X.691 10.3), so the
effective PER constraint is the parent's (1..128,...). The missing extension
bit shifts all following bits; asn1c failed to decode a POIM ParkingAvailability
message that Marben and the producer encode with the bit.

Fix: skip _remove_extensions() when the component constraint consists only
of component relation / table constraints (ACT_CA_CRC).

Effect on ETSI 2026 generated code (only PER constraints change):
  AsnWrappedPoiInformationBlock.c  poiType  (1..128)  -> (1..128,...)
  AsnInformationContainer.c        (IVI)    (0..127)  -> (0..127,...)
  AsnWrappedExtensionContainer.c            (1..16)   -> (1..16,...)

Apply: git apply patches/0001-keep-extensibility-for-table-constrained-class-fields.patch

diff --git a/libasn1fix/asn1fix_constraint.c b/libasn1fix/asn1fix_constraint.c
index c2f6e054..5190b6f1 100644
--- a/libasn1fix/asn1fix_constraint.c
+++ b/libasn1fix/asn1fix_constraint.c
@@ -7,6 +7,17 @@ static int constraint_type_resolve(arg_t *arg, asn1p_constraint_t *ct);
 static int constraint_object_resolve(arg_t *arg, asn1p_value_t *value);
 static int constraint_value_resolve(arg_t *arg, asn1p_value_t **value, enum asn1p_constraint_type_e real_ctype);
 
+static int
+_only_table_constraints(const asn1p_constraint_t *ct) {
+	unsigned int i;
+	if(!ct) return 0;
+	if(ct->type == ACT_CA_CRC) return 1;
+	if(ct->type != ACT_CA_SET || ct->el_count == 0) return 0;
+	for(i = 0; i < ct->el_count; i++)
+		if(!_only_table_constraints(ct->elements[i])) return 0;
+	return 1;
+}
+
 int
 asn1constraint_pullup(arg_t *arg) {
 	asn1p_expr_t *expr = arg->expr;
@@ -103,8 +114,10 @@ asn1constraint_pullup(arg_t *arg) {
 	if(ct_parent) {
 		/*
 		 * If we have a parent, remove all the extensions (46.4).
+		 * A table constraint alone is not PER-visible and keeps them.
 		 */
-		_remove_extensions(arg, ct_parent, 0);
+		if(!_only_table_constraints(ct_expr))
+			_remove_extensions(arg, ct_parent, 0);
 
 		expr->combined_constraints = ct_parent;
 		if(ct_expr->type == ACT_CA_SET) {
